        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ludwig van Beethoven, Heinrich August Marschner\n- Works: Turkish March (Marcia alla turca)\n- Roles: composer, pianist\n- Topics: German opera, classical march\n\nFacts:\n- Ludwig van Beethoven was baptised on 17 December 1770 and died on 26 March 1827.\n- Ludwig van Beethoven was a German composer and pianist.\n- Heinrich August Marschner was born on 16 August 1795 and died on 14 December 1861.\n- Heinrich August Marschner was the most important composer of German opera between Weber and Wagner.\n- The Turkish March, also called Marcia alla turca, is a well-known classical march theme by Ludwig van Beethoven.",
